{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01393",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 7.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.96,
      "end_seconds": 12.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "perfect, thanks hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 17.86,
      "end_seconds": 21.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "thank you for fitting us in, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.5,
      "end_seconds": 27.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "it's pain going into my left arm, mostly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.4,
      "end_seconds": 31.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.38,
      "end_seconds": 45.84,
      "duration_seconds": 12.46,
      "text": "Ever since... since this morning, really. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.6,
      "end_seconds": 51.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "right, is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.78,
      "end_seconds": 56.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "it comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.93,
      "end_seconds": 60.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.53,
      "end_seconds": 63.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Mild, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.55,
      "end_seconds": 68.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.7,
      "end_seconds": 98.49,
      "duration_seconds": 29.79,
      "text": "Well, uh, it usually comes with crushing chest pain. I mean, and I've been feeling sick as well, for about three months. The, The crushing chest pain? That's been for four weeks. So, as for crushing chest pain, it happens all the time. Uh, I've also been sweating, for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 99.47,
      "end_seconds": 116.08,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Height 172 centimetres, BMI works out to to 26.0, oxygen saturation is 96 percent, temperature is 36.8 degrees, pressure 130 over 76, heart rate 111, weight 77 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.67,
      "end_seconds": 117.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.09,
      "end_seconds": 122.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.77,
      "end_seconds": 125.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.86,
      "end_seconds": 144.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "You are pale and sweaty, and your pulse is fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.64,
      "end_seconds": 155.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Any fever or leg swelling at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.17,
      "end_seconds": 162.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Uh, um, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.68,
      "end_seconds": 164.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Have you had any cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.42,
      "end_seconds": 167.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "nope, no cough"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.12,
      "end_seconds": 170.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.51,
      "end_seconds": 173.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.33,
      "end_seconds": 185.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Alright, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.91,
      "end_seconds": 188.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.62,
      "end_seconds": 190.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "right, right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.14,
      "end_seconds": 195.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.0,
      "end_seconds": 205.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.69,
      "end_seconds": 221.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.33,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.37,
      "end_seconds": 230.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.67,
      "end_seconds": 235.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 237.61,
      "end_seconds": 246.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Actually, uh, I remember she had some kind of reaction to amoxicillin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.83,
      "end_seconds": 251.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Uh, really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.15,
      "end_seconds": 257.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.08,
      "end_seconds": 271.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.93,
      "end_seconds": 276.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 278.81,
      "end_seconds": 290.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.07,
      "text": "So, doctor, I think the last prescription for the amlodipine was 2.5 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.27,
      "end_seconds": 295.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.52,
      "end_seconds": 309.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "No, um, I left it at home. Atorvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.0,
      "end_seconds": 332.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like a possible heart attack. We shouldn't forget unstable angina."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.32,
      "end_seconds": 337.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "I mean, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.35,
      "end_seconds": 370.38,
      "duration_seconds": 31.03,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a possible heart attack, but I'd like to confirm i think a troponin blood test makes sense here, for chest pain it's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture let's get an ECG, for chest pain what I'm giving you is aspirin, 300 milligrams, once now, single dose it's for possible heart attack stay lying down and do not eat or drink"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.45,
      "end_seconds": 386.06,
      "duration_seconds": 13.61,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's review you straight away. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.6,
      "end_seconds": 391.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Um, great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.11,
      "end_seconds": 394.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}